PentaX modifications, 2026: explicit known register state, complete flat-stream
admission before resource reads, checked guest addresses and owned snapshots,
bounded termination walking through the real decoder, compiler arena/work
limits, typed unsupported paths, manifest-derived push data and opaque prepared
compute products. The separate stateful command planner adds bounded owned
indirect call/chain frames, active-cycle detection, multiple dispatch snapshots
and explicit known queue register history. Ordered owned memory-write/wait
actions, immediate completion labels, execution-time indirect dimensions and
empty dispatch outcomes preserve bounded synchronous ordering. Unfulfilled waits
remain distinct stops; interrupts and asynchronous scheduling are not imitated.
Acyclic wave32, raw single-buffer
compute is admitted; shader loops, conditional packets, asynchronous scheduling
and broader GPU state remain gaps. Tests are original, not game data.
The original flat inspector remains separately scoped original PentaX code.
